# Loaded by `next build` — which is BOTH deployed environments, since the
# DigitalOcean dev environment is also a production build.
#
# That is why neither variable is set here: one value would apply to both, and a
# dev dashboard silently pointing at the prod control plane is the worst outcome
# available. Each Cloudflare Pages project sets them, and a process env var
# beats this file.
#
#   dev   NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTROL_API_URL=https://api-control.dev.talqing.com
#         NEXT_PUBLIC_REGIONS=[{"slug":"in","name":"India (Bangalore)","api_url":"https://api-in.dev.talqing.com","default":true}]
#
#   prod  NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTROL_API_URL=https://api.control.talqing.com
#         NEXT_PUBLIC_REGIONS=[{"slug":"in","name":"India (Bangalore)","api_url":"https://api.in.talqing.com"},{"slug":"us","name":"United States (San Francisco)","api_url":"https://api.us.talqing.com","default":true}]
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_REGIONS is only the fallback: the live list comes from
# `GET /v1/regions` on the control plane and is cached in localStorage, so
# adding a region needs no dashboard deploy.
#
# See ./README.md.
